脸颊更红润一点。

526
00:18:49.240 --> 00:18:51.460
And her hair is just a little brighter red.
头发的红色也更鲜艳一点。

527
00:18:51.700 --> 00:18:52.480
You know what I'm saying?
你明白我的意思吗？

528
00:18:52.680 --> 00:18:56.340
It's just like, you just turn it up a couple of notches on the dial and you get Amy AdaMs.
就像是把刻度盘往上调了几档，就变成了艾米·亚当斯。

529
00:18:56.480 --> 00:18:59.120
Like if you're creating me, right, you get to me.
比如你在创造我的时候，对吧，创造出了我。

530
00:18:59.220 --> 00:19:02.540
And then if you turn the dial a couple more notches, it turns into Amy AdaMs.
然后如果你再把刻度盘往上调几档，就变成了艾米·亚当斯。

531
00:19:03.540 --> 00:19:04.440
She's Disney you.
她是迪士尼版的你。

532
00:19:04.760 --> 00:19:05.540
She kind of is.
她确实有点像。

533
00:19:05.580 --> 00:19:07.140
She's the Disney princess version of me.
她是迪士尼公主版的我。

534
00:19:07.300 --> 00:19:07.600
Yes.
没错。

535
00:19:07.840 --> 00:19:08.900
Angela, do you have a note card?
安吉拉，你有笔记卡吗？

536
00:19:09.000 --> 00:19:10.740
Because you're like handling a note card right now.
因为你现在好像拿着一张笔记卡。

537
00:19:10.820 --> 00:19:12.240
I feel like you want to say a note card.
我觉得你想说点笔记卡上的内容。

538
00:19:12.400 --> 00:19:13.040
I mean, I have a lot.
我是说，我有很多。

539
00:19:13.040 --> 00:19:14.880
It's in your hand and then you're touching them.
它就在你手里，你还在摸它们。

540
00:19:15.060 --> 00:19:16.060
What is it that you want to say?
你到底想说什么？

541
00:19:16.560 --> 00:19:18.500
Are you annoyed that I'm touching my note cards?
你是因为我在摸笔记卡而感到烦躁吗？

542
00:19:18.500 --> 00:19:21.220
No, I'm giving you a chance to speak.
不，我是在给你说话的机会。

543
00:19:21.800 --> 00:19:22.120
Oh.
噢。

544
00:19:23.500 --> 00:19:26.500
Oh, thank you so much.
噢，太感谢了。

545
00:19:26.740 --> 00:19:31.240
Oh, so it's British when you were offended.
噢，所以你被冒犯的时候就会用英式口音。

546
00:19:31.560 --> 00:19:31.920
Oh, God.
天哪。

547
00:19:32.120 --> 00:19:32.800
No, stop.
不，停下。

548
00:19:33.080 --> 00:19:33.300
Stop.
停下。

549
00:19:33.720 --> 00:19:38.520
I was just going to say that Michael Scott has a talking head that I love so much.
我只是想说，迈克尔·斯科特有一个我非常喜欢的访谈片段。

550
00:19:38.640 --> 00:19:42.800
And these are just one of these talking heads that they're in every episode and getting to
这些访谈片段每一集都有，而且能让人……

551
00:19:42.800 --> 00:19:43.480
rewatch them.
重温它们。

552
00:19:43.620 --> 00:19:45.620
I'm like, ah, my God, that's brilliant.
我当时就想，天哪，这太棒了。

553
00:19:45.920 --> 00:19:47.100
Is it the small businessman?
是关于那个小企业主的吗？

554
00:19:47.420 --> 00:19:48.000
I love it.
我喜欢这个。

555
00:19:48.160 --> 00:19:48.980
Is it the things that he reads?
是他读的那些东西吗？

556
00:19:48.980 --> 00:19:53.220
I love that he said he loves American Way magazine, the in-flight magazine.
他说他喜欢《美国之路》杂志，就是那种机上杂志，我太喜欢这一点了。

557
00:19:53.380 --> 00:19:58.160
And then he goes, they did a great profile on Doris Roberts and where she likes to eat
然后他说，他们对多丽丝·罗伯茨做了一篇很棒的专访，介绍了她喜欢去哪里吃饭，

558
00:19:58.160 --> 00:19:59.200
when she's in Phoenix.
当她在凤凰城的时候。

559
00:19:59.500 --> 00:20:02.240
It just made me laugh so hard because I read those.
这让我笑得不行，因为我也看那些杂志。

560
00:20:02.240 --> 00:20:06.800
I just want you to know, American Airlines, whenever I fly with you, I get the American
我想让你知道，美国航空，每当我乘坐你们的航班时，我都会拿出一本《美国之路》，

561
00:20:06.800 --> 00:20:09.140
way out and I look to see where people eat.
看看大家都在哪儿吃饭。

562
00:20:09.480 --> 00:20:10.840
It made me laugh so hard.
这真的让我笑得好开心。

563
00:20:10.960 --> 00:20:12.600
And then he's like, illuminating.
然后他说，很有启发性。

564
00:20:12.980 --> 00:20:14.660
I love those magazines, too.
我也很喜欢那些杂志。

565
00:20:14.840 --> 00:20:15.800
I read them.
我也会看。

566
00:20:16.120 --> 00:20:19.640
And, you know, actually, one of the coolest things that ever happened to me is that one
而且，你知道吗，其实我经历过最酷的事情之一就是有一次，

567
00:20:19.640 --> 00:20:22.240
time I had an article in...
我有一篇文章登在……

568
00:20:22.240 --> 00:20:23.400
In an in-flight magazine?
登在机上杂志里？

569
00:20:23.560 --> 00:20:23.740
Yes.
是的。

570
00:20:23.840 --> 00:20:25.900
Just like the Doris Roberts thing, I got profiled.
就像多丽丝·罗伯茨那样，我也被采访了。

571
00:20:26.220 --> 00:20:26.500
What?
什么？

572
00:20:26.700 --> 00:20:26.900
Yeah.
是啊。

573
00:20:27.080 --> 00:20:28.200
I would be so excited.
我会兴奋死的。

574
00:20:28.340 --> 00:20:29.140
Why didn't you tell me?
你为什么没告诉我？

575
00:20:29.220 --> 00:20:29.900
That is so cool.
那太酷了。

576
00:20:30.080 --> 00:20:33.600
No, I told this story about playing poker in Scotland.
不，我讲的是关于在苏格兰打扑克的故事。

577
00:20:34.080 --> 00:20:35.140
Oh, wait, wait.
哦，等等，等等。

578
00:20:35.200 --> 00:20:36.680
I know this is a total tangent.
我知道这完全跑题了。

579
00:20:37.040 --> 00:20:37.740
Guys, I'm sorry.
伙计们，抱歉。

580
00:20:37.880 --> 00:20:40.100
I have to take Jen on a tangent because I love this story.
我得带珍跑个题，因为我太喜欢这个故事了。

581
00:20:40.420 --> 00:20:41.120
Should I tell the story?
我该讲这个故事吗？

582
00:20:41.180 --> 00:20:42.220
You have to tell it.
你一定要讲。

583
00:20:42.380 --> 00:20:42.520
Okay.
好吧。

584
00:20:42.520 --> 00:20:44.980
Because, first of all, it makes you sound way cooler than you are.
因为首先，这让你听起来比实际酷多了。

585
00:20:45.060 --> 00:20:45.500
No offense.
别介意啊。

586
00:20:45.780 --> 00:20:46.180
I know.
我知道。

587
00:20:46.220 --> 00:20:47.700
But it kind of makes you sound like a rock star.
但这让你听起来有点像摇滚明星。

588
00:20:47.700 --> 00:20:49.940
Biggest rock star moment of my life.
那是我人生中最摇滚的时刻。

589
00:20:50.060 --> 00:20:50.780
It was pretty.
真的很赞。

590
00:20:50.780 --> 00:20:51.480
A hundred percent.
百分之百。

591
00:20:51.620 --> 00:20:51.800
Okay.
好吧。

592
00:20:52.020 --> 00:20:53.320
So, I had no...
所以，我当时没……

593
00:20:53.320 --> 00:20:57.020
I know you're going to tell that story, but I need to see that in-flight magazine article.
我知道你要讲那个故事，但我得看看那篇机上杂志的文章。

594
00:20:57.020 --> 00:20:57.480
I'll show it to you.
我会给你看的。

595
00:20:57.580 --> 00:20:58.740
It was for United.
那是为美联航写的。

596
00:20:59.020 --> 00:20:59.320
Okay.
好的。

597
00:20:59.480 --> 00:20:59.860
Magazine.
杂志。

598
00:21:00.500 --> 00:21:05.840
And they had this story where they wanted people to tell the craziest ways they've ever
他们当时有个专题，想让人们分享自己克服时差最疯狂的方法，

599
00:21:05.840 --> 00:21:06.880
fought jet lag.
克服时差。

600
00:21:07.100 --> 00:21:07.340
Okay.
好的。

601
00:21:07.560 --> 00:21:11.740
So, Lee and I had this little romantic trip that we took to Scotland.
我和李之前去苏格兰进行了一次浪漫的小旅行。

602
00:21:11.740 --> 00:21:13.260
This was before we had children.
那是在我们有孩子之前。

603
00:21:13.520 --> 00:21:16.820
I remember this because you told me you were going and I was like, well, that's not
我记得这件事，因为你当时告诉我你们要去，我心想，那时间也太

604
00:21:16.820 --> 00:21:17.880
a lot of days.
短了吧。

605
00:21:18.160 --> 00:21:18.460
Yeah.
是啊。

606
00:21:18.560 --> 00:21:21.780
We only had five days because we had a one-week hiatus from work.
我们只有五天时间，因为工作刚好有一周的空档。

607
00:21:21.900 --> 00:21:23.540
This is what people without children can do.
这就是没孩子的人能做的事。

608
00:21:23.700 --> 00:21:23.820
Yeah.
没错。

609
00:21:23.960 --> 00:21:27.700
They can just jet off to Scotland for five days.
他们说走就走，去苏格兰玩个五天。

610
00:21:27.980 --> 00:21:30.680
So, we were going to spend two days in Edinburgh.
所以，我们打算在爱丁堡待两天。

611
00:21:31.020 --> 00:21:31.180
Okay.
好的。

612
00:21:31.180 --> 00:21:33.940
And then we were going to go into the countryside for the other three days.
然后剩下的三天去乡下转转。

613
00:21:34.480 --> 00:21:38.380
Do a tour of a, you know, like a Scotch factory and everything.
去参观一下威士忌酒厂之类的，体验一下全程。

614
00:21:38.620 --> 00:21:38.670
Yeah.
嗯。

615
00:21:38.670 --> 00:21:39.000
Really fun.
真的很有趣。

616
00:21:39.000 --> 00:21:42.520
So, we get there and we thought we will take an overnight flight.
我们到了那里，本以为可以坐夜间航班过去。

617
00:21:42.580 --> 00:21:48.440
We will sleep on the plane and we will arrive at noon rested and ready to tour Edinburgh.
我们在飞机上睡觉，中午抵达时就能休息好，准备开始游览爱丁堡。

618
00:21:48.800 --> 00:21:49.440
Yeah, right.
是啊，想得美。

619
00:21:49.680 --> 00:21:50.660
This did not happen.
结果根本没成。

620
00:21:50.660 --> 00:21:53.660
We did not sleep on the plane and we landed.
我们在飞机上根本没睡着，飞机落地了。

621
00:21:53.660 --> 00:22:00.020
It was noon and we were thinking, how in the world are we going to make it through this
当时是中午，我们就在想，到底该怎么撑过

622
00:22:00.020 --> 00:22:00.520
whole day?
这一整天呢？

623
00:22:00.620 --> 00:22:01.540
We were exhausted.
我们精疲力竭。

624
00:22:01.560 --> 00:22:02.360
So tired.
太累了。

625
00:22:02.360 --> 00:22:03.680
We're touring a castle.
我们去参观城堡。

626
00:22:04.100 --> 00:22:05.740
We're walking along little shops.
我们逛着那些小店。

627
00:22:05.860 --> 00:22:10.560
We bought some hats at a little hat shop.
我们在一家小帽子店买了几顶帽子。

628
00:22:10.700 --> 00:22:11.120
Oh, wait.
噢，等等。

629
00:22:11.200 --> 00:22:11.440
I know.
我知道。

630
00:22:11.500 --> 00:22:11.720
I know.
我知道。

631
00:22:11.800 --> 00:22:16.400
I'm raising my hand because, Jenna, you texted me and I remember you saying, we're so tired.
我举手是因为，珍娜，你当时给我发短信，我记得你说，我们太累了。

632
00:22:16.400 --> 00:22:17.800
We're going to try to power through.
我们打算硬撑过去。

633
00:22:18.000 --> 00:22:20.480
We're going to try to power through so we don't fall asleep.
我们打算硬撑过去，这样就不会睡着了。

634
00:22:20.640 --> 00:22:20.880
Yes.
没错。

635
00:22:21.220 --> 00:22:22.780
You can't fall asleep in the middle of the day.
你不能在大白天睡着。

636
00:22:22.880 --> 00:22:23.460
Then you're ruined.
不然就全毁了。

637
00:22:23.700 --> 00:22:27.160
Then the whole five days, you're just going to be sleeping during the day and up at night.
那样接下来的五天，你白天只会想睡觉，晚上却清醒着。

638
00:22:27.160 --> 00:22:32.640
So it's five o'clock and we are so exhausted, just so incredibly exhausted.
当时是五点钟，我们已经累坏了，简直是累到极点。

639
00:22:32.800 --> 00:22:34.240
We thought, here's what we're going to do.
我们想，我们这样安排吧。

640
00:22:34.420 --> 00:22:36.180
We're going to go into a little pub.
我们找个小酒馆进去。

641
00:22:36.820 --> 00:22:38.300
We're going to get a bite to eat.
吃点东西。

642
00:22:38.660 --> 00:22:39.860
We're going to have a drink.
喝上一杯。

643
00:22:40.040 --> 00:22:43.940
We are going to force ourselves to stay awake until 7 p.m.
我们要强迫自己撑到晚上七点。

644
00:22:44.180 --> 00:22:46.820
And then we're going to go back to the hotel and fall asleep.
然后我们就回酒店睡觉。

645
00:22:47.020 --> 00:22:47.140
Right.
对。

646
00:22:47.240 --> 00:22:47.900
That was your plan.
这就是你们的计划。

647
00:22:48.080 --> 00:22:50.640
Go to the pub, power through, and then go to bed.
去酒馆，硬撑着，然后去睡觉。

648
00:22:50.840 --> 00:22:51.240
Correct.
没错。

649
00:22:51.640 --> 00:22:52.740
We get to the pub.
